# OWB firmware build environment — WiFi credentials and optional overrides.
#
# Usage:
#   cp .env.example .env
#   # edit .env with your actual credentials
#   source .env
#
# NEVER commit .env — it is listed in .gitignore.
# The build scripts and Docker cross-compile both read these from the environment.

# ----- STA (station) credentials -----
# The bot will attempt to join this network on boot.
# Leave blank to skip STA and go straight to SoftAP fallback.
OWB_WIFI_SSID=your-network-name
OWB_WIFI_PASSWORD=your-network-password

# Legacy bare names (also accepted by the build scripts and owb-esp.rs):
# SSID=your-network-name
# PASSWORD=your-network-password

# ----- SoftAP fallback -----
# When STA is blank or fails, the bot brings up a WPA2 access point.
# Defaults: SSID=OWB-BOT, no password (open AP requires OWB_ALLOW_OPEN_AP=1).
# AP_SSID=OWB-BOT
# AP_PASSWORD=your-ap-password

# ----- Control secret (C1) -----
# Optional pre-shared key for WebSocket/BLE control transport.
# Empty = unauthenticated (dev/bench only — do not use in production).
# CONTROL_KEY=your-control-key

# ----- Bench overrides -----
# Force SoftAP even when SSID is set:
# OWB_FORCE_SOFTAP=1
#
# Allow an open (no-password) SoftAP on a bench bot:
# OWB_ALLOW_OPEN_AP=1
